{
  "base": "AI-ERP",
  "currencySymbol": "₪",
  "_notes": [
    "Single source of truth for the ERP: the 8 Airtable tables, their fields and their types. Build the base from this file.",
    "Field 'type' is a small logical vocabulary that maps to an Airtable field type: text, longtext, email, phone, url, int, currency, percent, date, datetime, checkbox, select, created.",
    "Relationships are plain string foreign keys (e.g. CustomerId = 'CUST-0001'), not Airtable links.",
    "'created' fields are Airtable 'Created time' fields. Airtable's API cannot create these — add them once in the UI (see docs/01-airtable.md). The Airtable Triggers need them.",
    "The first field in each table is the primary field.",
    "percent values are fractions: 0.18 means 18%."
  ],
  "tables": [
